//
//  TWO LEVELS, and the difference matters:
//    SUSPECT -- this reading, right now, cannot be trusted.  Set on the FIRST bad
//               sample so the page never renders a fault code as degrees.  It is
//               not an alert; a single glitch trips it and clears again.
//    FAULT   -- untrusted for 5 consecutive minutes.  This is the one that means
//               'send a technician', and it clears after 5 good minutes.
//
//  anyTemperatureProbeDead is set when a side has BOTH channels bad at once.
//  Humidity corroborates 998/999 at 97 % and the -46.8 rail at 99.9 %, but the
//  high rail at 0 % -- so both-channels-bad means the probe is not responding,
//  while temperature alone means one corrupted I2C transaction.  See 018 3.4.
